---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const lastUpdated = "2026-04-28";
---
<Base title="privacy — velocit.ee" description="Privacy notice for velocit.ee. What we collect, what we don't, and how to ask us to forget you.">
  <article>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-wrap px-6 lg:px-10 py-16">
      <p class="label">// legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-mono text-4xl text-cream tracking-tightest">privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-2xs font-mono text-muted">last updated · {lastUpdated}</p>

      <section class="mt-10 prose">
        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          velocit.ee is a marketing site for an open-source project. We are deliberately
          minimal in what we collect:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Waitlist email addresses</strong>, when you give them to us. Stored in our own
            PostgreSQL database. Used to email you when we have something relevant to share.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact form submissions</strong> — the message contents you send, plus your
            email address so we can reply. Routed to <code>inquiries@velocit.ee</code> and stored
            in that mailbox.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Hashed IPs</strong> for rate-limiting. We hash incoming IP addresses with HMAC-SHA-256
            before storing them. Raw IPs never hit disk.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Aggregate request logs</strong>, kept for 30 days for debugging and abuse handling. No tracking cookies.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>What we don’t collect</h2>
        <p>
          No analytics. No third-party scripts. No tracking pixels. No advertising IDs. We don't
          fingerprint visitors, we don't sell mailing lists, and we don't share data with anyone
          we haven't told you about below.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong> — for sending email (waitlist updates, contact form replies, transactional notifications).</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — provides the tunnel that exposes velocit.ee publicly. They process request metadata as a CDN.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>That's it. No analytics providers, no ad networks, no third-party "consent management".</p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          velocit.ee operates from Germany — the GDPR applies. You can ask us to delete your data,
          export everything we have on you, or correct anything that's wrong, by emailing
          <a href="mailto:inquiries@velocit.ee">inquiries@velocit.ee</a>. We aim to reply within 7 days.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact for privacy questions</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:legal@velocit.ee">legal@velocit.ee</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
